  "findings": [
    "Restored Porterfield #2835–Stephenson Island access map with both required dam carries explicit. The 2017 FERC assessment describes the portages; Article 409 of the 2018 license requires maintenance.",
    "Current DNR dam records, FERC facility map and satellite context match Third Marinette to Park Mill and First/Lower Marinette to Menominee, both project 2744. Current operator page corroborates ownership and joint license. Its recreation table has blank cells here and is not used to claim current portage conditions.",
    "Four upstream river overviews added after all 23 course panels and eight endpoint panels passed review. The complete 290-feature named-and-unnamed source has no alternative downstream branches for these pairs.",
    "Six current DNR boat-access records have ABANDON_FLAG No. Existing facility-area markers and precision are retained. Porterfield #2835 coordinate attributes and GIS geometry differ slightly; the existing approximate area remains beside the river rather than being promoted to an exact landing.",
    "The other Menominee dam holds remain. Evidence for these two lower dams does not resolve Grand Rapids or the full Little Quinnesec/Sturgeon Falls itinerary."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Published agency evidence and imagery are desktop review, not a current field inspection. Confirm signed carry approaches, closures and boat suitability.",
    "No exact carry lines, landing connectors or continuous dotted paths through the dams are mapped.",
    "No point coordinates, stable IDs, numeric planning miles, gauges or timing modes changed.",
    "New dotted courses are display-only, with no GPS remaining time, distance adoption or land overlay.",
    "No deployment, push or production changes."
  ]
